  "verdict": "Standard misalignment with the condensate's NATURAL decay constant (f ~ v/2 = 123 GeV) badly UNDER-produces: Omega \u221d f^2, so a low-scale f needs either a trans-Planckian mass (light mode) or relies on the heavy amplitude-mode freeze-out instead. A light axion-like angular mode reaches Omega_DM only if f is pushed to ~10^15-10^16 GeV (intermediate/GUT), far above the E_g condensate scale. The relic obstruction is therefore SHARPENED, not closed: misalignment alone fails by the f-scale gap. The heavy AMPLITUDE mode via thermal freeze-out DOES reach Omega_DM in the WIMP window, so the E_g sector's dark-matter relic is the heavy amplitude mode, not the light angular one (updating the F197 candidate identification)."
